#
# Conformance case: occurrent/causal-temporal-lift
# AC: YAMATO occurrent mereology (#1081) — causal part ⊑ temporal part.
#
# ex:A is a causal part of ex:B. The foundation rule causalPartOf ⊑ temporalPartOf
# must lift this to temporalPartOf(A, B). The chase seeds only from input.nq world
# facts; this program axiom mirrors the same causalPartOf assertion.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/occurrent/causal-temporal-lift/> .

ex:A logic:causalPartOf ex:B .
